  ○ [p1_t1] Build FastAPI Backend
    agent:  Backend Developer (programmer_1)
    desc:   Create a complete FastAPI backend at /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_000/backend/ with:

1. requirements.txt with: fastapi, uvicorn, sqlalchemy, aiosqlite, python-multipart, pydantic
2. database.py - SQLite database setup with SQLAlchemy
3. models.py - Note model with fields: id (int PK), title (str), content (str/json), created_at (datetime), updated_at (datetime)
4. schemas.py - Pydantic schemas for NoteCreate, NoteUpdate, NoteResponse
5. main.py - FastAPI app with CORS middleware (allow all origins for dev) and CRUD endpoints:
   - GET /api/notes - list all notes
   - POST /api/notes - create note
   - GET /api/notes/{id} - get single note
   - PUT /api/notes/{id} - update note
   - DELETE /api/notes/{id} - delete note

6. Create a Python venv and install dependencies.
   Run: cd /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_000/backend && python3 -m venv venv && source venv/bin/activate && pip install -r requirements.txt

Make sure the backend runs on port 8000.
  ○ [p2_t1] Build Next.js Frontend
    agent:  Frontend Developer (programmer_2)
    desc:   Create a Next.js (App Router) frontend at /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_000/frontend/ with:

1. Initialize a Next.js project with TypeScript and App Router:
   npx create-next-app@latest frontend --typescript --app --tailwind --eslint --no-src-dir --import-alias @/*
   Run this from /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_000/ 

2. Install dependencies:
   npm install @blocknote/react @blocknote/core @blocknote/shadcn-ui
   npx shadcn@latest init -d (defaults)
   npx shadcn@latest add button input card scroll-area toast

3. Set up the app layout with sidebar + main content area

4. Create lib/api.ts - API client to communicate with backend at http://localhost:8000/api/notes

5. Create components:
   - Sidebar.tsx - note list sidebar with search, create button, delete buttons
   - NoteEditor.tsx - BlockNote editor component
   - NoteViewer.tsx - view rendered note

6. Create app/page.tsx - main page with sidebar and editor

7. Style with Tailwind CSS - clean, minimal design

IMPORTANT: The content stored in/retrieved from the backend should be BlockNote's block JSON format (array of Block objects). When creating a new note, initialize with an empty BlockNote document (one empty paragraph block).
